From 10fe37a058590648a2d4af6a8a7aa77baadacafe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wai Chung <351198037+ternii-ai@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 08:26:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ggml-cuda: kernels for the dense trit types TQ9_128 /
 TQ27_128 / TQ81_128

Adds CUDA support for the three dense trit types:

- tq.cuh / tq.cu: dequantisation (bit-identical to the CPU reference) and
  a decode mat-vec for 1-8 activation columns, used for MUL_MAT and
  MUL_MAT_ID (expert id read on the device, so CUDA graphs keep working).
  Activations stay f32 (no q8_1 step).
- convert.cu: to_fp16 / to_fp32 / to_bf16 (+ non-contiguous) for the
  cuBLAS path used above 8 columns (prompt processing).
- getrows.cu: GET_ROWS.
- ggml-cuda.cu: routing (TQ never goes to MMVQ / MMQ, which have no TQ
  kernels), supports_op, and no stream sync for MUL_MAT_ID at <= 8 tokens.
- test-backend-ops: Qwen3.6-35B-A3B decode shapes in the perf suite.
- tools/tq_exact: dequantises every TQ tensor of a GGUF on CUDA and compares
  it bitwise with the CPU reference.

No MMQ kernel yet: prompt processing uses dequantise + cuBLAS.
